{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/molliecomponents"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"MollieComponents","externalID":"MollieComponents","modules":[{"name":"MollieComponents"}]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"MollieComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the merchant-facing entry point to the Mollie Components iOS SDK. You present a payment surface — modal or embedded — hand it a server-issued client access token, and receive a single typed ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/mollie-components-2-ios-sdk.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/MolliePaymentResult","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" describing how the flow ended. The card number and CVC the cardholder types are captured inside Mollie’s own UI and tokenized over TLS; they never cross the documented SDK boundary into your code. Your ","type":"text"},{"code":"onResult","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" callback receives only session metadata, never raw card data.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"3D Secure is handled for you. When the issuer requires a challenge, the SDK presents the authentication WebView, drives it to a terminal state, and folds the outcome back into the same ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/mollie-components-2-ios-sdk.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/MolliePaymentResult","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" you already handle — there is no separate 3DS callback to wire up.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The SDK runs inside your app’s process. UIKit provides no platform-level isolation between your code and the SDK, so the protection of typed card data is "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"contractual, not platform-enforced"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":". Read "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SECURITY.md"},{"type":"text","text":" at the repository root for the full trust model — what the SDK defends against, what it cannot enforce, and the integration practices your team must follow."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Important"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To get going in a few lines, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/mollie-components-2-ios-sdk.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/GettingStarted","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". To restyle the sheet to match your brand, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/mollie-components-2-ios-sdk.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/Theming","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". To map every outcome the SDK can hand back to merchant-facing behavior, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/mollie-components-2-ios-sdk.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/HandlingErrors","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/mollie-components-2-ios-sdk.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Accept card payments in your iOS app with a drop-in, PCI-aware payment UI — card tokenization, 3D Secure, and theming behind a single import."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Getting Started","identifiers":["doc:\/\/mollie-components-2-ios-sdk.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/mollie-components-2-ios-sdk.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/MolliePaymentSheet"],"anchor":"Getting-Started"},{"title":"Presenting","identifiers":["doc:\/\/mollie-components-2-ios-sdk.MollieComponents\/documentation\/MollieComponents\/MolliePaymentSheet","do